  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Tunisian NDI Semianr 01-22</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of this program is to provide a foundation for NDI participants, as senior military and civilian officials and civil society representatives, to help the Tunisian Government address challenges faced by the country during their continued transition and to help insure the durability of the governance system adopted through the Tunisian political process. Subject areas will include whole of government and whole of society processes and policies to speak to both hard and soft security challenges arising from regional threats such as the conflict in Libya, the roll of international players, and spill over from the Sahel. In addition, the goal is to challenge their assumptions and traditional ideas of threats to security and the state, such as water and food security, climate change, pandemics, and transitional threats. Significant seminar content will be developed based on the specific research theme assigned to the NDI class by the Tunisian Minister of Defense.</narrative>
  </description>
